arest work. Agents choose and adapt mechanisms from local evidence.\"\n      },\n      \"research_budget\": {\n        \"seconds\": 172800,\n        \"start_event\": \"dataset_download_and_checksum_verification_completed\",\n        \"start_unix\": 1793959348.3455288,\n        \"deadline_unix\": 1794132148.3455288\n      },\n      \"test_policy\": \"closed during research; any final suite must be frozen before held-out scoring\",\n      \"source_sha256\": {\n        \"baseline.py\": \"f4b473cbacf60d72cff90f3721ad754dd617ee6065fe3fca2fc9cd4be2b25c36\",\n        \"train.py\": \"e81bdefa140a4d78cae12f4123cc421611109c84da1b9f067e23d11b6c3d335a\",\n        \"visibility.py\": \"d1f641c62fa3c72e1eadc03aad6d999cc9af87fceb783775eb22d1405d9ac6b4\",\n        \"data.py\": \"ef28cb65880b6931d3e567d2bfb4a67d7530c18067b68e47bf483b65b2560438\"\n      },\n      \"upstream_commit\": \"90bb99a60724e975ec565836266fd86dcad0039d\",\n      \"benchmark_deviations\": [\n        \"DIN is the initial empirical reference; unified research candidates can use entirely different architectures.\",\n        \"One GPU per model; batch8192 per model (single-device rather than published distributed global batch).\",\n        \"Click AUC selects models, four-task mean AUC is auxiliary.\",\n        \"Validation includes every sample; upstream default drop_last may omit remainders.\",\n        \"In-process DataLoader (num_workers=0): container shared memory is512MiB; all compared runs use the same loading policy.\",\n        \"No torch.compile; BF16; TF32 disabled.\"\n      ],\n      \"trial_cap_seconds\": 1203.3689693547785,\n      \"estimated_unit_seconds\": 481.3475877419114,\n      \"estimated_validation_seconds\": 75.22459795698524,\n      \"frozen_unix\": 1793961097.640512,\n      \"identity\": \"1a10f150c0b3977043072cd01f67a339c5c476f15c7847d04fa3acf9ce71e216\"\n    },\n    \"method\": \"auto\",\n    \"budget_scope\": \"The research wall clock starts at the recorded dataset download/checksum completion. Earlier acquisition and setup costs are reported separately; every later preparation step, calibration, agent call, failure, training/control and scoring job counts.\",\n    \"no_test_feedback\": true,\n    \"knowledge_revision\": \"knowledge-access-v3\",\n    \"knowledge_review\": {\n      \"policy\": \"Evaluate relevant external references against local evidence; adoption is optional. Missing source detail and negative transfer remain explicit.\",\n      \"proposal_output\": \"Add top-level knowledge_assessments: [{knowledge_id, decision: used|considered|rejected|unresolved, rationale, transformed_mechanism, variant_names, nearest_work_difference, falsifier}]. Cover retrieved industry cards; identify the concrete changed mechanism for used cards. This is provenance, not causal proof.\",\n      \"reflection\": \"Review the latest knowledge-usage.json alongside outcomes; distinguish declared use, executed changes, mechanism evidence and unresolved attribution.\"\n    },\n    \"latest_knowledge_usage\": null\n  },\n  \"study_schema\": {\n    \"$schema\": \"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema\",\n    \"title\": \"Task-independent prospective mechanism study\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"additionalProperties\": false,\n    \"required\": [\n      \"id\",\n      \"protocol_ref\",\n      \"evidence_refs\",\n      \"question\",\n      \"hypothesis\",\n      \"nearest_work\",\n      \"inherited_components\",\n      \"proposed_difference\",\n      \"predictions\",\n      \"falsifiers\",\n      \"alternative_explanations\",\n      \"contrasts\",\n      \"cost_plan\"\n    ],\n    \"properties\": {\n      \"id\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"minLength\": 1\n      },\n      \"protocol_ref\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"minLength\": 1\n      },\n      \"evidence_refs\": {\n        \"type\": \"array\",\n        \"minItems\": 1,\n        \"items\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"question\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"minLength\": 1\n      },\n      \"hypothesis\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"minLength\": 1\n      },\n      \"nearest_work\": {\n        \"type\": \"array\",\n        \"minItems\": 1,\n        \"items\": {\n          \"type\": \"object\",\n          \"additionalProperties\": false,\n          \"required\": [\n            \"source_ref\",\n            \"verification\",\n            \"difference\"\n          ],\n          \"properties\": {\n            \"source_ref\": {\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            },\n            \"verification\": {\n              \"enum\": [\n                \"discovered\",\n                \"read\",\n                \"archived\",\n                \"implementation_checked\"\n              ]\n            },\n            \"difference\": {\n              \"type\": \"string\",\n              \"minLength\": 1\n            }\n          }\n        }\n      },\n      \"inherited_components\": {\n        \"type\": \"array\",\n        \"items\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"proposed_difference\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"minLength\": 1\n      },\n      \"predictions\": {\n        \"type\": \"array\",\n        \"minItems\": 1,\n        \"items\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"falsifiers\": {\n        \"type\": \"array\",\n        \"minItems\": 1,\n        \"items\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"alternative_explanations\": {\n        \"type\": \"array\",\n        \"minItems\": 1,\n        \"items\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"contrasts\": {\n        \"type\": \"array\",\n        \"minItems\": 1,\n        \"items\": {\n          \"type\": \"object\",\n          \"additionalProperties\": false,\n          \"required\": [\n            \"parent_ref\",\n            \"intervention\",\n            \"control\",\n            \"held_fixed\",\n            \"remaining_confounds\",\n            \"decision_if_supported\",\n            \"decision_if_not_supported\"\n          ],\n          \"properties\": {\n            \"parent_ref\": {\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            },\n            \"intervention\": {\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            },\n            \"control\": {\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            },\n            \"held_fixed\": {\n              \"type\": \"array\",\n              \"items\": {\n                \"type\": \"string\"\n              }\n            },\n            \"remaining_confounds\": {\n              \"type\": \"array\",\n              \"items\": {\n                \"type\": \"string\"\n              }\n            },\n            \"decision_if_supported\": {\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            },\n            \"decision_if_not_supported\": {\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            }\n          }\n        }\n      },\n      \"cost_plan\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"additionalProperties\": false,\n        \"required\": [\n          \"estimate_ref\",\n          \"all_variants_counted\",\n          \"attribution_reserve\",\n          \"assessment_reserve\",\n          \"stop_rule\"\n        ],\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"estimate_ref\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"all_variants_counted\": {\n            \"const\": true\n          },\n          \"attribution_reserve\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"assessment_reserve\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"stop_rule\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          }\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  \"required_study_protocol_ref\": \"1a10f150c0b3977043072cd01f67a339c5c476f15c7847d04fa3acf9ce71e216\",\n  \"reference_format\": \"Use allowed_observation_ids verbatim for local evidence. Descriptive references are accepted when they contain a complete known ID. Correct any previous_runtime_error before submitting; its failed costs remain charged.\",\n  \"action\": \"Read candidate.py and baseline_reference.py, diagnose an observed limitation, check primary nearest work, and implement a feasible candidate. Write proposal.json containing study (matching study_schema), parent_trial (existing trial ID), and variants (1-4 objects with distinct name, file basename ending .py, role candidate/control, config object, and note). At least one candidate is required. Add key ablations or matched controls for the claimed mechanism when feasible; reference existing matched trials as controls where justified. Each variant is a standalone module. Do not run training. New architecture choices come from evidence; industry cards do not mandate them.\",\n  \"candidate_api\": {\n    \"Model\": \"Model(feature_map, model_id=..., gpu=0, **kwargs) -> torch.nn.Module; optional MultiTaskModel utilities. forward(inputs) returns {label+\\\"_pred\\\": probability [B,1]} for all four tasks. Host places the module on the assigned GPU.\",\n    \"architecture_scope\": \"Whole-model design for unified modeling. Model need not inherit the initial reference, retain its pooling, or use separate task towers; representations, interactions, routing and readout can all be replaced.\",\n    \"lineage\": \"parent_trial records the empirical comparison and evidence lineage. A complete rewrite may have no inherited architectural components.\",\n    \"proposal_unit\": \"Coordinated structural changes implementing one coherent mechanism are allowed; isolate their effects through planned replacement, component or factorial controls.\",\n    \"meta\": \"Read-only UniRank FeatureMap: features (ordered specs, sources, vocab_size), labels, data_dir. Full framework reference files are available through tools.py.\",\n    \"batch\": [\n      \"inputs=(batch_dict,item_dict,history_mask,multi_task_history_masks)\",\n      \"batch_dict: categorical user/context features int64[B]; current labels and lookup metadata are removed by host\",\n      \"item_dict: item_id,cate_id,campaign_id,customer_id,brand,price_bucket,action, each int64[B,101]; last position is current target, preceding100 are pre-padded history\",\n      \"history_mask: float 0/1 [B,100]; four task masks: [B,100]; use only masked history\",\n      \"Target action is always zero (unknown/padding), never a current label. Historical feedback policy is frozen in protocol.history_policy.\",\n      \"Historical item_id is a previous advertisement ID. Shopping events used to create auxiliary labels are only matched by user/category/brand.\",\n      \"No raw timestamps, event-time deltas, raw user IDs, full future histories, current labels or global sample indexes are supplied to forward.\"\n    ],\n    \"task_labels\": [\n      \"is_click\",\n      \"cart\",\n      \"fav\",\n      \"buy\"\n    ],\n    \"primary\": \"Validation is_click ROC-AUC. All four AUC/Logloss values and mean AUC are reported; auxiliary mean is not the selection score.\",\n    \"optional\": [\n      \"Literal CONFIG dict for model architecture only; all frozen host parameters are rejected.\",\n      \"Model.training_loss(inputs, probabilities[B,4], train_labels[B,4]) -> finite differentiable scalar; labels supplied only during training. Default is sum of four unweighted BCEs.\"\n    ],\n    \"ownership\": \"Edit candidate modules/proposal only. No filesystem/network operations in model source. Imports: torch,numpy,math,typing,copy,functools,collections,itertools,dataclasses,contextlib,unirank,model_zoo. Host owns training, input filtering and scoring.\",\n    \"local_checks\": \"Coding jail has no torch; check syntax/source there. Host trains and scores. Do not install or train inside coding jail.\",\n    \"training\": \"From scratch; same frozen data, seed, epochs, batch, history limit and dense AdamW / embedding Adagrad. Architecture may be rewritten completely. Retain causal controls and account for added parameters/computation.\"\n  }\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
