{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_42","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport ast, hashlib, json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nsource=Path('candidate.py').read_text()\nvariants=[]\nfor name,file,field,group,role in [\n ('field_feedback','candidate.py',True,True,'candidate'),\n ('event_feedback','control_event_feedback.py',False,True,'control'),\n ('field_global','control_field_global.py',True,False,'control'),\n ('event_global','control_event_global.py',False,False,'control')]:\n    text=source.replace(\\\"'field_retrieval': True, 'feedback_groups': True\\\",f\\\"'field_retrieval': {field}, 'feedback_groups': {group}\\\")\n    text=text.replace('field_retrieval=True, feedback_groups=True,',f'field_retrieval={field}, feedback_groups={group},')\n    if file\"'!='\"'candidate.py': Path(file).write_text(text)\n    tree=ast.parse(text)\n    cfg=next(ast.literal_eval(n.value) for n in tree.body if isinstance(n,ast.Assign) and any(isinstance(t,ast.Name) and t.id=='CONFIG' for t in n.targets))\n    variants.append(dict(name=name,file=file,role=role,config=cfg,\n        note=f'2x2 study: field_retrieval={field}, feedback_groups={group}. Identical tensor shapes, counts, absence flags, static skip path, optimizer recipe and interaction stack across all four variants. Source SHA256 '+hashlib.sha256(text.encode()).hexdigest()+'.'))\nstudy={\n 'id':'field-feedback-representation-factorial-v1',\n 'protocol_ref':'1a10f150c0b3977043072cd01f67a339c5c476f15c7847d04fa3acf9ce71e216',\n 'evidence_refs':['baseline-din','baseline_reference.py SHA256 f4b473cbacf60d72cff90f3721ad754dd617ee6065fe3fca2fc9cd4be2b25c36','framework:unirank/pytorch/dataloaders/unirank_dataloader.py lines 383-408, 525-577','unirank-code:HiFormer lines 113-159','unirank-code:EST lines 119-216','unirank-code:TokenFormer lines 117-155'],\n 'question':'Does preserving field-specific relevance inside feedback-conditioned historical summaries improve joint field/history/task modeling beyond the same architecture using event-wide relevance and whole-history summaries?',\n 'hypothesis':'The inspected DIN adaptation assigns one target-only weight to each concatenated exposure, includes historical action only in values, and supplies one summary to every task. This can average together category/brand/advertisement relevance and rare feedback evidence. A target/context-conditioned score for each item field, normalized within each of four overlapping host feedback masks plus an all-exposure group, may retain complementary evidence before joint static-field/summary/task interaction. This is a provisional mechanism, not an observed failure of DIN.',\n 'nearest_work':[\n  {'source_ref':'paper:din; archived primary text content-sha256 5fee25f33f375e51b3ee9417d376ff9dbe2ea3628c932a7679ddfeb0feaaade2 lines 219-277','verification':'read','difference':'Inherits field embeddings and target-conditioned retrieval concept. Uses normalized field-specific and feedback-conditioned summaries with explicit count features, rather than unnormalized local activation over concatenated events. This is not an exact DIN reproduction.'},\n  {'source_ref':'unirank-code:HiFormer at 90bb99a60724e975ec565836266fd86dcad0039d lines 113-159; paper:hiformer original text unavailable through registry','verification':'implementation_checked','difference':'Nearest stacked alternative: pooled history plus field/task tokens. Proposed difference is the field-by-feedback retrieval factorization before a small shared attention stack. Does not reproduce hierarchical low-rank heterogeneous HiFormer blocks. Original-method novelty remains unverified.'},\n  {'source_ref':'unirank-code:EST at 90bb99a60724e975ec565836266fd86dcad0039d lines 119-216; paper:est original text unavailable through registry','verification':'implementation_checked','difference':'Shares use of identifiable fields and sequence retrieval, but summarizes history once into five tokens and does not iteratively update event tokens or use EST per-token FFNs. No full-method superiority claim.'},\n  {'source_ref':'unirank-code:TokenFormer at 90bb99a60724e975ec565836266fd86dcad0039d lines 117-155; paper:tokenformer original text unavailable through registry','verification':'implementation_checked','difference':'Shares field/history/target interaction motivation; compresses the fixed visible history before interaction instead of retaining all events in full/sliding-window attention. Not a reproduction or verified original contribution.'}\n ],\n 'inherited_components':['Frozen four-label sample interface, released item/action embeddings (dimension 16), official_offline history and fixed host training recipe.','FeatureEmbeddingDict, MultiTaskModel input filtering, Dice tower activations and separate binary readouts from the existing adaptation.','Established target-aware pooling, field tokens, learned task queries, residual self-attention and feed-forward blocks as architectural concepts; new implementation does not copy benchmark model code.'],\n 'proposed_difference':'Replace DIN local activation and its single history summary with a representation study: six actual item fields are pooled using field-specific relevance within five groups (all visible exposures plus the four supplied feedback masks). Concatenate pooled field subvectors and an action subvector, project each group to width 32, add its log-count and identity, and jointly interact with separately projected static user/context/target fields and four task tokens through two small attention blocks. Query uses target field and mean user/context embeddings. No timestamps or current labels enter forward; target action is never read. All four variants include the same five count features, raw static skip path and summary/tower architecture. Event controls average field relevance logits before pooling; global controls replace group retrieval masks by whole-history masks but preserve actual counts and group absence flags. Thus factor comparisons isolate retrieval factorization, not the entire replacement relative to DIN. No positional modeling is claimed in this first study.',\n 'predictions':[\n  'Primary predeclared comparison: field_feedback click AUC exceeds event_global on the full 2,871,767-sample validation. A gain over DIN alone does not identify either proposed factor.',\n  'Field factor: field_feedback-event_feedback and field_global-event_global have positive click AUC differences; feedback factor: field_feedback-field_global and event_feedback-event_global have positive differences. Report all four differences and the interaction (field_feedback-event_feedback)-(field_global-event_global), including negative values.',\n  'Secondary expectation: feedback grouping better preserves auxiliary-task AUC and unweighted logloss, but click AUC remains the selection criterion; do not substitute mean-task AUC.',\n  'Exploratory history-length diagnostics use existing empty/1-16/17-64/>64 bins with sample, positive and negative counts. Grouping should chiefly affect nonempty histories; empty-history differences can reflect training-mediated changes and are not direct retrieval effects. Baseline slice AUC differences are not causal evidence of dilution.',\n  'All four factorial variants must have exactly equal embedding and dense parameter counts. Measured training, inference throughput, p50/p95 whole-batch latency, peak memory, examples and allocated GPU seconds must be reported; similar dimensions do not establish equal wall time.'\n ],\n 'falsifiers':[\n  'No advantage over event_global, or an advantage confined to DIN comparison, fails to support the combined field/feedback retrieval explanation.',\n  'If field-only or group-only replacements match or outperform the combined candidate, narrow or reject the interaction hypothesis; retain that simpler trajectory as a candidate.',\n  'If event controls match field-specific models at identical parameter counts, field-specific relevance is unsupported in this implementation. If global controls match grouped variants while counts remain available, separate feedback summaries are unsupported.',\n  'Nonfinite forward/backward results, sensitivity to masked field/action IDs, incorrect four-output shapes, nonzero summary from all-masked input, or access to current target action invalidates execution and requires correction before interpreting metrics.',\n  'A failed or timed-out implementation is an execution/resource outcome, not a refutation of the representation mechanism. A single seed is preliminary; a later paired repetition reversing gains weakens support.'\n ],\n 'alternative_explanations':[\n  'Relative to DIN, normalized weights, explicit counts, static skip connections, context-conditioned retrieval, task tokens, shared interactions, parameter count and optimization all change. Only within-factorial contrasts attribute field or feedback retrieval effects.',\n  'Grouping introduces a useful inductive constraint and different effective rank even with identical trainable tensors. Equal nominal parameters do not equate optimization or functional capacity.',\n  'The shared event score is an additive aggregate of field logits, not a reproduction of DIN nonlinear concatenated-event attention. Results concern this controlled replacement, not every possible event encoder.',\n  'Group summaries overlap for composite action tokens; they are not independent behaviors. Rare auxiliary outcomes match user/category/brand within 24 hours and are not advertisement-level conversions.',\n  'Offline delayed feedback visibility, inherited whole-window filtering/vocabularies, time shift and single-pass optimization may affect any benefit. There is no established production point-in-time validity.',\n  'The mean context query and low-dimensional pooled group bottleneck may underfit; a negative result cannot exclude finer field-group tokens or iterative retrieval. No sequence-order dependency is represented.',\n  'The only committed trajectory is baseline-din: click AUC 0.6555440824200336, logloss 0.18339680255790589, 32,059,429 total/266,213 dense parameters, 328.9133 seconds wall, 4,196,814,848 peak GPU bytes. No failed, abandoned or competing local trajectories are supplied; external cards are not local successes.'\n ],\n 'contrasts':[\n  {'parent_ref':'baseline-din','intervention':'field_feedback full replacement versus DIN reference','control':'Committed baseline-din with matched frozen seed/data/recipe, plus event_global as closest new architecture control.','held_fixed':['Dataset identity 9f110bfc2f037f36e2f48787b812df640fe5df2de1cda8db7ac04590c1c9be44','All visibility, labels, split, scoring and host optimizer/precision contracts','One epoch, batch 8192, history 100, seed 20262027'],'remaining_confounds':['DIN versus replacement changes several components and dense parameter count; this comparison measures model performance, not mechanism attribution.','A committed reference is not a new paired seed; repeat candidate and closest control before repeated-support claims.'],'decision_if_supported':'Retain predictive improvement provisionally, inspect factorial attribution and measured quality/cost; do not label it novel or significant.','decision_if_not_supported':'Retain DIN and inspect all factorial outcomes, cost, rare-group sparsity and training stability before deciding whether a discriminating follow-up is warranted.'},\n  {'parent_ref':'baseline-din','intervention':'2x2 field_retrieval x feedback_groups, all four cells','control':'event_global (False,False), event_feedback (False,True), field_global (True,False), field_feedback (True,True)','held_fixed':['Same source body except two architecture flags/defaults','Identical parameter tensors, module construction/initialization order and embedding dimensions','Same target/context query, action values, group counts/absence flags, static field tokens, two interaction blocks, task readouts and loss','Frozen full-data training recip